#: ../../reference/reason-codes.rst:114
msgid ""
"The *Next step* column names what the sentence asks of the reader. "
"``command`` rows give the command, with its placeholders. The other "
"values are ``none needed``, ``auto`` (the node is handling the matter), "
"``retry later``, ``change input`` (change the request, an argument, a "
"file or the condition of the node, then repeat), ``contact`` (ask the "
"other side or an operator), ``start over`` (create a new task) and "
"``futile`` (repeating the request does not help)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/reason-codes.rst:124
msgid "Codes that are not shown"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/reason-codes.rst:126
msgid ""
"Some conditions are handled by the node and have no sentence: an expired "
"hub session that the daemon reopens, a stale encryption key identifier "
"that the outbound engine re-wraps, replayed or stale request timestamps "
"that the daemon signs again, and the many lower-case, hyphenated "
"rejection counters of the sealed-envelope layer. These are counted and "
"written to the log. They do not appear in ``anet.reason``, in a control-"
"plane ``reason`` or in an ``ErrorInfo``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/reason-codes.rst:133
msgid ""
"Rejections of the ANetLink C1 interface are mapped to user codes and are "
"not exposed: ``not_permitted`` is reported as ``provider_policy``, "
"``unknown_capability`` and ``not_found`` as ``capability_not_served``, "
"``too_large`` as ``args_too_large``, and ``bad_request``, "
"``unsupported_media``, ``internal`` and ``c1_version`` as "
"``backend_failed``."
msgstr ""

